#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Verbal_Instructions_V3.py  -  Camera-guided patient intake with recorded voice prompts + on-screen text

What changed from V2
  * NEW: PatientDisplay shows every spoken prompt as large, high-contrast text on a second
    (patient-facing) monitor, synced to the moment each clip starts. Edit the wording in CAPTIONS.
    Corrections show in yellow, success in green. The operator window (camera + overlay) is unchanged.

What changed from V1
  * Text-to-speech is replaced by clips cut from V1_Patient_Prompts.mp3 (see CLIPS).
  * The simulated sensor flags are replaced by real detection: body pose (MediaPipe) on the
    Orbbec color stream, plus the aligned depth stream for distance to the camera.
  * time.sleep() is gone. Audio plays in the background, so video never freezes and the
    system never talks over itself.
  * Movement-based corrections: feet apart, arms away from sides, slouching, and moving
    during the measurement each trigger their own recorded correction clip.
  * Audio clips are available three ways: play (VoicePlayer), get (AudioClipLibrary.get),
    or export to WAV files (--export-clips DIR).

Install
  pip install pyorbbecsdk2 mediapipe opencv-python pygame numpy
  (MediaPipe >= 0.10.30 removed the old "solutions" API. This script supports both. With a
   newer MediaPipe, download pose_landmarker_lite.task and pass --pose-model path/to/it.)

Run
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py                    # Orbbec camera, shows a window
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --source webcam    # test with a normal webcam
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --preview          # play every clip + its text in order, no camera
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --export-clips clips/
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --display-index 1  # put the patient text on monitor 2
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --patient-windowed # patient text in a window (testing)
  python Verbal_Instructions_V3.py --no-patient-display
  Press Esc in the patient display window to quit.
  Press q in the video window (or Ctrl+C) to quit.
"""
